        "action:n11",
        "guard:b2->n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Upon finding reusable ideas from previous campaigns, we create a new concept."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional premise is modeled as an action (n9) and branch (b2). The positive guard and primary action (n10) match exactly. The secondary path (n11, b2->n11) is a redundant restatement permitted by the redundancy rule."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the new concept is created, we integrate new ideas and add further points."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase preserving all components."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Next, we integrate the revised campaign into the database."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match of the integration step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The concept is then presented to the relevant party for consideration."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithful restatement of the presentation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15",
        "guard:b3->n16",
        "action:n16",
        "guard:b3->n17",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the concept is declined, we rework it. On the other hand, if the concept is accepted, we proceed to present it to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional is modeled as an action (n15) leading to a branch (b3). Both arms are correctly guarded (No/Ys) and mapped to their respective actions (rework/present)."
    },
    {
